---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Trip Leaders & Local Partners',href:'/trip-leaders-partners/'}];
const roles=[
 {title:'Talon Trip Planners',sub:'Overall trip design & coordination',image:images.planning},
 {title:'Destination Operators',sub:'Local logistics & ground handling',image:images.road},
 {title:'Guides & Activity Specialists',sub:'Route, technical & local expertise',image:images.trekking},
 {title:'Instructors',sub:'Skill-based travel & progression',image:images.surf},
 {title:'Hosts & Community Leaders',sub:'Group-facing support & coordination',image:images.group},
 {title:'Cruise, Marine & Hospitality',sub:'Coast, island & comfort travel',image:images.boat}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Trip Leaders, Guides & Local Partners | Talon Expeditions" description="How Talon Expeditions works with trip planners, destination operators, guides, instructors, hosts, cruise partners, and local specialists to support group travel worldwide." image={images.trekking} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="av-inner-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.trekking}')`}><div class="shell"><h1>Our Team</h1><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="av-services-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Meet the Team Around the Trip</p><h2>Passionate People and Specialists Behind Better Group Travel</h2><p>Talon Expeditions coordinates travel through internal planning, organizer relationships, destination operators, guides, instructors, hosts, and activity-specific specialists. The exact team changes with the itinerary rather than pretending one staff roster performs every job everywhere.</p></div><div class="av-team-grid">{roles.map((role)=><article class="av-team-card" style={`background-image:url('${role.image}')`}><div class="av-team-social"><i>↗</i></div><div class="av-team-label"><strong>{role.title}</strong><span>{role.sub}</span></div></article>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="av-category-stage"><div class="shell av-category-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Who Leads What</p><h2 class="section-title">Choose the Right Capability for the Itinerary</h2><p class="av-category-copy">A credible group travel plan should be clear about who is responsible for each important part of the trip.</p><ul class="av-category-menu"><li>Trip Planning</li><li>Destination Operations</li><li>Guiding</li><li>Instruction</li><li>Hosting</li><li>Hospitality</li></ul></div><div class="av-category-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.water}')`}><div class="av-category-caption"><h3>Global planning. Local capability.</h3><p>A mountain route, dive program, cruise, city experience, or remote transfer depends on people who understand that place and activity.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="av-why-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">Selection Principles</p><h2>Partner Fit Should Be Specific to the Actual Trip</h2></div><p>A supplier being excellent in one context does not make them right for every group. Capacity, qualifications, communication, pace, equipment, language, accessibility, schedule, and contingency options all matter.</p></div><div class="av-why-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}></div><div class="av-why-grid"><div class="av-why-item"><div class="av-why-item-head"><h3>Capability & Qualification</h3><span class="num">01</span></div><p>Technical or regulated activities should use appropriately qualified providers and comply with local operating requirements.</p></div><div class="av-why-item"><div class="av-why-item-head"><h3>Group Fit</h3><span class="num">02</span></div><p>Guide ratios, language, pace, equipment, flexibility, and communication need to work for the actual travelers.</p></div><div class="av-why-item"><div class="av-why-item-head"><h3>Operational Fit</h3><span class="num">03</span></div><p>Supplier timing, transport, accommodation, activities, and contingency have to connect with the wider itinerary.</p></div><div class="av-why-item"><div class="av-why-item-head"><h3>Clear Roles</h3><span class="num">04</span></div><p>Travelers should know where Talon, the organizer, the local operator, the guide, and the instructor each fit.</p></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
